---
description: |
  Deduplicates HarfangLab Module Activity (`class_uid` 1005) per window, host,
  and module file. Events of other classes pass through unchanged.

  The first load of every module file in a window passes through immediately
  and unchanged, with the loading process and the base address. Further loads
  of the file in the same window are repeats: when the window closes, one
  summary event stands for them, and a file without repeats gets no summary.
  A summary is a Module Activity event with the OCSF aggregation attributes:
  `count` holds the number of repeats, which excludes the first load,
  `start_time` and `end_time` the times of the first and last repeat,
  `duration` the time between them, and `time` equals `start_time`. All times
  are epoch milliseconds, like HarfangLab's. Only summaries have `count`.

  The key covers the module file's path, name, size, hashes, and signature,
  so another binary at the same path gets its own summary. The base address
  differs between loads and doesn't appear in a summary. HarfangLab
  identifies the loading process mostly by its process ID alone. A summary
  keeps the process ID, name, and path of the loading process only if all
  repeats came from the same one, and `unmapped.distinct_pids` holds the
  number of distinct loading process IDs. A summary of repeats from several
  processes has an empty `actor.process`, while OCSF requires the actor to
  name at least a process or a user.

  Windows close on the wall clock every `window`, and every summary covers at
  most one `window` of event time. The package description explains the
  windowing and how a SIEM counts summaries.
args:
  named:
    - name: window
      type: duration
      default: 1d
      description: Width of the deduplication windows, in processing and event
        time.
---

if class_uid == 1005 {
  _host = device?.agent_list?[0]?.uid? else device?.hostname?
  _bucket = from_epoch(time? * 1ms).floor($window)
  _hashes = module?.file?.hashes?
  _md5 = _hashes.where(h => h.algorithm_id == 1).first().value?
  _sha1 = _hashes.where(h => h.algorithm_id == 2).first().value?
  _sha256 = _hashes.where(h => h.algorithm_id == 3).first().value?
  window size=$window {
    // A digest of the keys keeps the state of the first-occurrence check
    // small. The summary below groups by the same keys.
    _key = hash_md5([_host, _bucket, module?.file?.path?, module?.file?.size?,
      _sha256, _sha1, _md5, module?.file?.signature?.state_id?,
      module?.file?.signature?.certificate?.serial_number?])
    summarize _key, _seen=count(), options={mode: "cumulative"}
    if _seen == 1 {
      drop _key, _host, _bucket, _hashes, _md5, _sha1, _sha256, _seen
    } else {
      // All keys are scalars. The records come from the first repeat: the
      // device and metadata belong to the host, the module file to the keyed
      // path, hashes, and certificate.
      summarize _host, _bucket, activity_id?, activity_name?, type_uid?,
        severity_id?, severity?,
        module?.file?.path?, module?.file?.name?, module?.file?.size?,
        _md5, _sha1, _sha256, module?.file?.signature?.state_id?,
        module?.file?.signature?.certificate?.serial_number?,
        module?.load_type_id?, module?.load_type?, module?.type?,
        module?.function_name?,
        count=count(), start_time=min(time?), end_time=max(time?),
        _device=first(device?), _metadata=first(metadata?),
        _file=first(module?.file?),
        _pids=count_distinct(actor?.process?.pid?),
        _pid=min(actor?.process?.pid?),
        _pid_count=count(actor?.process?.pid?),
        _names=distinct(actor?.process?.name?),
        _name_count=count(actor?.process?.name?),
        _paths=distinct(actor?.process?.file?.path?),
        _path_count=count(actor?.process?.file?.path?)
      _pid = _pid if _pids == 1 and _pid_count == count else null
      _name = (_names[0]
        if _names.length() == 1 and _name_count == count else null)
      _path = (_paths[0]
        if _paths.length() == 1 and _path_count == count else null)
      this = {
        activity_id: activity_id,
        activity_name: activity_name,
        category_uid: 1,
        class_uid: 1005,
        metadata: _metadata,
        severity: severity,
        severity_id: severity_id,
        time: start_time,
        start_time: start_time,
        end_time: end_time,
        duration: end_time - start_time,
        count: count,
        type_uid: type_uid,
        // OCSF requires the actor, so it stays even when nothing about the
        // loading process holds for all repeats.
        actor: {
          process: {
            file: {path: _path} if _path != null else null,
            name: _name,
            pid: _pid,
          },
        },
        device: _device,
        module: {...module, file: _file},
        unmapped: {distinct_pids: _pids},
      }
      drop_null_fields
    }
  }
}
